cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "When a fourth prime-race crossing gives new elliptic points"
abstract: "Four first-crossing targets with rational squares give exact ranks of zero, two or four modulo constant points on V^2 = U^3 - U. For a fixed triple every extra rational target individually leaves the entire group unchanged. Two specified rational targets together raise the rank from two to four."
